Conclusion

-- Today I learned that eye tracking allows XR headsets to detect where the user is looking using infrared cameras and computer vision. I also learned that foveated rendering uses this 
information to render only the area of focus in high quality while reducing detail in the peripheral vision. Together, these technologies improve user interaction, graphics performance, and the overall immersive experience.
